# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Secrets — NEVER commit these
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Runtime artifacts
audit.log
*.log
demo/letter.html
demo/letter.pdf
demo/metrics.html

# Claude Code agent worktrees (harness scratch space, not repo content)
.claude/worktrees/

# Agent scratch space (pid files, throwaway drivers) — never repo content
.scratch/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Throwaway probe scripts and raw API dumps.
#
# Verifying a shape against the live API — rather than against src/remote/
# mockServer.js, which is what hid five defects on 2026-08-18 — means writing
# a one-off script and dumping the response. Those are working notes, not
# deliverables: the FINDING belongs in a test or in docs/, and the dump itself
# is a stale copy of an API that gets reseeded. .employments.json and
# .schemas.json are also raw Sandbox records, which prime directive 5 keeps
# out of the repo on principle even in a sandbox.
.probe*.mjs
.probe*.out
.employments.json
.schemas.json
.nld-schema.txt
.sandbox-cap/

# Built ZAF app bundles (`dist/zaf-app-<version>.zip`). The bundle is a zip of
# zaf-app/, rebuilt in one command — committing a binary that is derivable from
# tracked files is how the repo and the installed app come to disagree about
# which one is authoritative.
dist/

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/

# --- Local orchestration working files: never part of the portfolio -----------
# These are how the fleet works, not what it built. They are untracked today,
# which is one `git add -A` away from being public. Ignoring them is what
# actually keeps them out; making the repo private does not, because a repo can
# be flipped back to public and its history comes with it.
.gc/
.claude/skills/
.beads/formulas/
.beads/identity.toml
.beads/routes.jsonl
zaf-app/tmp/
# Repo-root scratch. Untracked and, until now, NOT ignored — agents' throwaway
# probes (tmp/vc33, tmp/zaf, tmp/zd, tmp/zafharness) sat one `git add -A` away
# from being committed. The pre-commit guard that used to catch that was retired
# 2026-08-23T21:45Z once the owner's outbox work was committed, so ignore it here.
tmp/

# Re-tuned demo receipts are generated against whatever the Sandbox holds
# TODAY (see scripts/make-demo-receipt.mjs --total/--date). The committed
# variants are the fixtures; these are scratch.
qa/fixtures/receipts/demo-receipt-tuned-*.pdf
